      "\"I think social care in England is as unfair as American healthcare,\" Burnham said in a speech outlining his pledge for reform on Wednesday. \"The vulnerable pay with everything and it can completely leave them with nothing.\"": "\"我认为英格兰的社会照护和美国医疗一样不公平，\"伯纳姆在周三阐述其改革承诺的演讲中说。\"弱势群体付出一切，而这可能让他们一无所有。\"",
      "Mary's late husband, Richard, was diagnosed with early onset Alzheimer's disease in 2015 at the age of 55. She had to quit her job as a fashion designer to care for him and paid for 15 hours of care a week, amounting to nearly £27,000 a year.": "玛丽已故的丈夫理查德在2015年、55岁时被诊断出早发性阿尔茨海默病。她不得不辞去时装设计师的工作来照顾他，并支付每周15小时的照护费用，一年接近2.7万英镑。",
      "\"I'm left with virtually no savings, living on my pension, working a bit and I have very good friends who I rent from,'\" says the 67-year-old from Kent. They had worked hard to build a good life, and it was frustrating to give it all up, she says. \"I'm a very positive, resilient person but I think I've been through a really ugly tunnel with very little help.\"": "\"我几乎身无积蓄，靠养老金生活，做点零工，而且我有很好的朋友，我向他们租房，\"这位来自肯特的67岁老人说。她说，他们曾努力建立美好的生活，放弃这一切令人沮丧。\"我是一个很积极、很有韧性的人，但我觉得我在几乎没有帮助的情况下走过了一条非常黑暗的隧道。\"",
      "She feels dementia - a terminal neurological disease - is neglected by the system. \"If it is not something you can give a drug to, you're swept aside. You have to sit quietly until you die and hope your friends and family look after you.\"": "她觉得痴呆症——一种终末期神经疾病——被这个体系忽视了。\"如果不是能用药物治好的病，你就会被扫到一边。你只能安静地坐着等死，指望你的朋友和家人照顾你。\"",
      "Annabel's 27-year-old son, Fred, lives independently with the support of carers who help with his daily living. His local council, North Somerset, charges him £147.54 a week from his benefits to pay for his care, leaving him with very little to live on.": "安纳贝尔27岁的儿子弗雷德在照护者的帮助下独立生活，照护者协助他的日常生活。他所在的北萨默塞特地方议会每周从他的福利金中扣除147.54英镑用于支付照护费用，让他所剩无几，难以维生。",
      "She believes the social care system needs proper government investment. \"Charging people on benefits for their care doesn't seem like a reasonable thing to be doing,\" she says.": "她认为社会照护体系需要政府适当的投入。\"向领福利的人收取照护费，似乎并不是一件合理的事，\"她说。",
      "Jayne's daughter Alice, 32, is autistic and has complex mental and physical health issues. Alice initially had care provided for her at home, which Jayne says was of \"very poor quality with little understanding of her autism\".": "杰恩32岁的女儿爱丽丝患有自闭症，并有复杂的心理和身体健康问题。爱丽丝最初在家接受照护，杰恩说那\"质量很差，对她自闭症几乎不理解\"。",
      "Jayne says she struggles to access emotional support, with charities overstretched. Her local carers' support organisation has had to reduce services, including scrapping its counselling service and cutting funding for hobbies and trips.": "杰恩说，由于慈善机构资源紧张，她很难获得情感支持。她当地的照护者支持组织不得不削减服务，包括取消心理咨询服务，并削减用于爱好和出游的经费。",
      "She thinks social care reform should be supported by an increase in tax. \"We shouldn't see it as money that results in nothing. We tend to forget about people who have a long-term disability or health issue,\" she says. \"There's an assumption that you're old and you sell your house to pay for it. It can happen to you at a much younger age.\"": "她认为社会照护改革应得到增税的支持。\"我们不应该把它看作打了水漂的钱。我们往往忘记了那些有长期残疾或健康问题的人，\"她说。\"人们有一种假设，认为你老了才会卖掉房子来支付照护费。但它也可能在你年轻得多的时候发生。\""
